            <ArticleTitle>Differentiation and treatment of phantom sensation, phantom pain, and residual-limb pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article defines the three major forms of postamputation sensation: 1) phantom sensation, 2) phantom pain, and 3) residual-limb pain. Proposed etiologies for phantom pain are discussed. The literature on current diagnoses and treatments for each of the three postamputation sensations is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
